[00:00.000]It has a pulse
[00:03.455]It has a name
[00:06.434]It speaks in tongues and goes by the name of pain
[00:10.844]It grows on vines
[00:13.098]The burning kind
[00:15.891]Where my body’s mine but my mind is the king
[00:22.709]Do you have the key?
[00:25.422]Can you set this tortured spirit free?
[00:30.042]Do you see the flame?
[00:32.759]Can you burn away my guilt and shame?
[00:37.261]Do you hear my plea?
[00:39.968]Can you break the chains surrounding me?
[00:46.796]Do you know the door?
[00:49.480]Can you keep me safe forevermore?
[01:13.184]It wears a mask
[01:15.529]It stalks the day
[01:18.547]It feeds on doubts that never fade away
[01:22.766]It moves through walls
[01:25.214]It drains the light
[01:27.891]Where my soul is weak but my fear is tight
[01:37.190]Do you have the key?
[01:39.857]Can you end this endless misery?
[01:44.547]Do you hold the cure?
[01:47.082]Can you make my shattered heart endure?
[01:51.556]Do you see the night?
[01:54.211]Can you guide me toward the morning light?
[02:01.196]Do you hear the call?
[02:03.943]Can you catch me when I start to fall?
